    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0251" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg155"/>

                <head>No. 97.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Hurlbut.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 26,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 60.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon further consideration of the case of
                    the Montijo in connection with your dispatch No. 73, it has occurred to me that
                    it might be advisable, before determining upon the course which this Government
                    ought to adopt in view of the denial of its accountability by the government of
                    Colombia, to give that government an opportunity to review its
                    determination.</p>
                <p>You will consequently inform that government of this disposition on our part;
                    that we have no interest in being at variance with Colombia, no feeling other
                    than a friendly one for her, but that we cannot forego the duty of requiring
                    her, as an independent power, to discharge her obligations as such to the United
                    States and their citizens.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
